## 16. API Best Practices

- Always check HTTP response status.
- Handle failed requests using try/catch.
- Validate API response data.
- Avoid unnecessary API requests.
- Cache gold prices according to the provider's update interval.
- Avoid requesting daily exchange rates repeatedly.
- Display the actual update timestamps.
- Use HTTPS endpoints.
- Never expose private API keys in frontend JavaScript.
- Follow API provider terms and attribution requirements.
- Do not assume API data is always available.

